  <section class="cho-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow"><em>Vibrio cholerae</em> · seven pandemics since 1817</span>
    <h1 class="disp">Curable in hours.<br><span class="gold">Never eradicated.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Cholera can kill a healthy adult in under half a day through dehydration alone — and has been reliably curable since the 1970s with a solution of clean water, sugar, and salt that costs pennies. It's also the disease that founded modern epidemiology, decades before anyone knew what caused it. We are currently living through its seventh pandemic, which began in 1961 and has never officially ended.</p>
    <div class="cho-hero-stats" aria-label="Cholera at a glance">
      <div><span class="n">7</span><span class="k">pandemics since 1817 — the seventh has run since 1961</span></div>
